WEBVTT

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:07.096
Captain's Log, Stardate 48623.5.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.632
There are 246 elements
known to Federation science.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.874
We believe we have
just discovered the 247th

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:18.247
inside the ring system
of a Class-D planet.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.684
The element has
an unusually large atomic mass...

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.449
over 550 nucleons.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.513
And the readings are constant.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.921
The element appears
to be stable.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:28.155
A stable, transuranic element
inside a natural environment.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.491
This is a first.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.394
Can you imagine what we
could make with this stuff?

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.559
Probe casings that could go
into the core of a sun.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.829
Ultrathin reactor shielding.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:36.893
That's assuming we can mine it.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:37.994
Ensign, try and locate

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.164
the highest concentration
of the element.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.230
The element is present

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.265
in most of the asteroids
that comprise the rings.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:46.574
I can isolate a sample
and beam it aboard.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.773
Or better yet,
maybe we could get

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:48.974
a first-hand look
at this element

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.846
in its natural environment.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.409
It looks like most
of these asteroids

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.353
support Class-M atmospheres.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.856
Good idea. Commander,
you're in charge.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:59.358
Aye, Captain.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.758
Mr. Kim, would you
like to join us?

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:03.422
I wouldn't miss it, sir.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.962
The highest concentration

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.435
is about 30 meters
directly ahead.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.064
I'm picking up
a large cavern in there.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.733
The readings are...

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.765
What the hell is this?

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.972
It's organic.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:23.813
Some kind of biopolymer residue.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.875
I want to see what's ahead.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.871
The readings are higher
over here,

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.669
but I still can't find
the source of the...

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.943
Commander?

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:02.015
Class-5 humanoid.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.683
It appears to be dead.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.768
Captain, there are
18 bodies here...

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.067
all humanoid...
11 male, seven female.

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:34.436
From what we can tell,

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:36.373
they're in various stages
of decomposition.

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:38.603
Some have been here for years.

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.839
Others, no longer
than a few days.

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:43.746
In fact, one body arrived
less than 12 hours ago.

00:04:43.782 --> 00:04:44.976
Arrived from where?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.176
I don't know, Captain,

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:47.879
but from the position
of the arms

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.150
I'd say we're looking
at some kind of burial site.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.487
What about the element
we discovered?

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:55.118
It's emanating
from their bodies, Captain.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.355
We think it's
some kind of byproduct

00:04:57.396 --> 00:04:59.591
of their decomposition process.

00:04:59.631 --> 00:05:02.566
I recommend we leave these
bodies in peace, Captain.

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.069
However, Mr. Kim
has a different opinion.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.662
With all due respect, Captain,

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.696
I have to disagree
with the Commander.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.335
This is our first contact
with this race,

00:05:11.376 --> 00:05:14.038
and I think we should be
learning all we can about them.

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:16.445
It's a unique
anthropological opportunity.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:17.676
I understand the chance

00:05:17.716 --> 00:05:19.274
for scientific discovery,
Captain,

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:22.253
but whatever belief this race
has, they clearly meant

00:05:22.287 --> 00:05:23.447
for their dead to be left alone,

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:24.956
and I think we should
respect that.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.049
I'm afraid
I agree with Commander Chakotay.

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:29.458
Set your tricorders
for passive scans.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.656
I don't want
to disturb anything.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:33.164
Captain, the sanctity

00:05:33.198 --> 00:05:35.564
of these bodies
should be respected.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.069
I recommend we make
visual observations only.

00:05:38.103 --> 00:05:39.400
No tricorders.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:40.962
Very well.

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:42.506
Keep me informed.

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:43.735
Janeway out.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:44.970
All right.

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:47.375
The only sensors you
have left are your eyes.

00:05:47.412 --> 00:05:48.538
Concentrate on details.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.979
We're going to have
to do a thorough report

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:53.279
when we get back.

00:05:53.318 --> 00:05:57.277
Commander, thanks for letting me
voice my opinion to the Captain.

00:05:57.322 --> 00:06:00.189
I remember the first time
I went on a tomb excavation

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:01.954
on Ktaria Vll.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.224
I wanted to keep a memento
of the experience,

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.322
so I picked up a rock
from the burial site.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:09.459
Only I found out later
it wasn't just a rock.

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.298
What was it?

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:13.133
It was a sacred stone.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:16.141
The Ktarians lay thousands
of them in the Tomb.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.507
Each one represents
a special prayer.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.034
Without realizing it,

00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:22.308
I had desecrated
that man's grave.

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:26.146
Well...

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:28.551
I think I've found out
about all I can with my eyes.

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:29.645
Really?

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:32.282
What have you learned
about this culture so far?

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:36.693
They like to bury their dead
on asteroids.

00:06:36.728 --> 00:06:39.663
That's about all I can tell
without a tricorder.

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:41.290
No artifacts, no inscriptions,

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:42.800
just some naked dead people.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:45.235
You're looking,
but you're not seeing.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.601
The fact that they're
naked says a lot.

00:06:46.638 --> 00:06:48.162
It means this race
doesn't believe

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:49.401
in dressing the deceased.

00:06:49.441 --> 00:06:51.807
And the lack of artifacts
could indicate

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:53.311
they don't believe
any worldly goods

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:55.779
can be taken into the afterlife.

00:06:55.814 --> 00:06:57.975
What makes you think
they believe

00:06:58.083 --> 00:06:59.641
in an afterlife at all?

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:02.620
Look at the position
of the arms and hands.

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:06.055
The bodies have been arranged
in poses of serenity,

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:08.286
and they appear to be wrapped
in the same biopolymer residue

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.056
we found out in the passageway...

00:07:10.095 --> 00:07:11.756
all indications
that this culture

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:13.162
has a great deal of ritual

00:07:13.198 --> 00:07:15.496
associated
with disposing of the dead.

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:18.526
That normally indicates
some belief in the afterlife.

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:20.765
The Klingons believe
in an afterlife,

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:22.569
but there's no burial ritual.

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.508
They just dispose of the corpse

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:25.942
by the most efficient
means possible.

00:07:26.044 --> 00:07:27.568
Good point.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.673
However, some archeological digs
on the Klingon Homeworld...

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.488
Tricorders.

00:07:37.522 --> 00:07:40.457
A dimensional distortion
is forming.

00:07:40.492 --> 00:07:42.551
Some kind of subspace vacuole.

00:07:42.594 --> 00:07:44.721
Chakotay to Voyager.
Emergency beam-out.

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:48.164
We're having trouble
locking on to your signals.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.167
Stand by.

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:50.600
Have everyone stand
closer together.

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.365
I'm going to try
a blind beam-out

00:07:52.404 --> 00:07:53.530
centered on your com signal.

00:07:53.572 --> 00:07:55.699
Acknowledged. Energize!

00:07:59.244 --> 00:08:02.042
Bridge to Transporter Room 3.
Do you have them?

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.810
Subspace distortions
from the vacuole are interfering

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:05.817
with the transporter lock.

00:08:05.851 --> 00:08:08.786
I'm attempting to compensate.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.720
Okay. I think I've got them.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.660
Chakotay and Lieutenant
Torres are aboard.

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:19.561
So is one
of the humanoid bodies,

00:08:19.598 --> 00:08:21.930
but there's no sign
of Ensign Kim.

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:24.265
Scan the asteroid.

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.271
No life signs, Captain.

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:28.034
I'm broadening the scan.

00:08:28.073 --> 00:08:29.540
Nothing.

00:08:29.574 --> 00:08:32.372
He is nowhere in the
entire asteroid field.

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:35.778
Seska, initiate Emergency
Transport Procedure 21 Alpha.

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:38.214
I'm already on it, Captain.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.217
It's no use.

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:40.616
His pattern's gone

00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:43.712
and the subspace vacuole
has disappeared.

00:08:43.755 --> 00:08:45.450
I'm looking
at the transporter logs.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.287
My only guess is he was
pulled into the vacuole.

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:49.590
This isn't one of the bodies
we found in the cavern.

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:50.595
It's someone else.

00:08:50.629 --> 00:08:52.961
This body might have come out
of the vacuole

00:08:53.065 --> 00:08:54.726
at the same time
Kim was taken in.

00:08:54.766 --> 00:08:55.858
Wait a minute.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:59.359
I'm showing signs of electrical
activity in the brain.

00:08:59.404 --> 00:09:01.338
It looks like she died
just a few minutes ago.

00:09:01.373 --> 00:09:03.603
We might be able to revive her.

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:06.440
If we can, we might
get some answers.

00:09:06.478 --> 00:09:07.672
We can't interfere

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:11.672
with this woman's
natural process of death.

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:14.083
What do you suggest we do,
Commander?

00:09:14.119 --> 00:09:15.552
Kim's gone.

00:09:15.587 --> 00:09:16.781
She's the only one
who might be able

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.687
to tell us what happened.

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:22.293
Beam us directly to Sick Bay.

00:09:22.327 --> 00:09:23.885
Aye, Commander.

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:26.794
Death is the end of this life,

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:30.700
but it is also the beginning
of a new journey.

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:35.070
Ptera will now thrive
in the Next Emanation.

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:39.203
This is both her sacred duty
and her great privilege.

00:09:39.244 --> 00:09:41.439
Eler'atah.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.539
As she begins her transition,

00:09:43.582 --> 00:09:45.948
we promise
to carry memories of her

00:09:46.018 --> 00:09:48.009
so that when we enter the...

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:51.956
Help! Get me out of here!

00:09:52.057 --> 00:09:54.082
She's... alive!

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:55.889
Deactivate the cenotaph...

00:09:55.927 --> 00:09:57.861
quickly!

00:09:57.896 --> 00:09:59.124
Let me out!

00:10:07.739 --> 00:10:09.570
Here it is.

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:11.735
Thanks.

00:10:13.745 --> 00:10:16.805
A lot of memories in this.

00:10:16.848 --> 00:10:19.840
We're so proud of you, Hatil.

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:22.445
This is such a generous,
selfless act.

00:10:22.487 --> 00:10:26.947
It's my last gift for you
and the children.

00:10:26.992 --> 00:10:29.085
And it's one we will
always cherish.

00:10:31.563 --> 00:10:34.123
But I'm still going to miss you.

00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:36.999
I know.

00:10:37.035 --> 00:10:39.026
I'll miss you, too.

00:10:41.406 --> 00:10:44.204
But I'll see you
in the Next Emanation,

00:10:44.242 --> 00:10:46.437
when you're ready to join me.

00:10:47.746 --> 00:10:49.907
Give my love to your father.

00:10:49.948 --> 00:10:53.281
Tell him that the
garili trees he planted

00:10:53.318 --> 00:10:56.913
have, have been in bloom
for three years straight.

00:10:56.955 --> 00:10:58.820
I will.

00:11:04.362 --> 00:11:08.162
- Good-bye.
- Good-bye.

00:11:26.818 --> 00:11:27.978
Lie down.

00:11:28.019 --> 00:11:29.987
It's going to be all right.

00:11:30.021 --> 00:11:32.012
We won't harm you.

00:11:34.392 --> 00:11:35.960
Who is that?

00:11:36.093 --> 00:11:38.118
We're not sure yet.

00:11:38.162 --> 00:11:41.154
We think he came
from the Next Emanation.

00:11:41.198 --> 00:11:43.962
The Next Emanation?

00:11:45.703 --> 00:11:47.898
You mean he's come back?

00:11:47.938 --> 00:11:49.405
Come back from where?

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.601
We've called
for the thanatologist.

00:11:51.642 --> 00:11:53.166
He'll be here any moment.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.438
I don't think there should be

00:11:54.478 --> 00:11:56.810
any further discussion
about this until he arrives.

00:12:08.659 --> 00:12:10.593
How did you get here?

00:12:12.863 --> 00:12:14.592
I'm not sure.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:21.362
I just sort of woke up
inside one of those pods.

00:12:21.405 --> 00:12:23.930
I was conducting
an investigation

00:12:23.974 --> 00:12:25.441
on an asteroid.

00:12:25.476 --> 00:12:26.966
We found some dead bodies.

00:12:27.011 --> 00:12:30.572
Then there was some kind
of subspace phenomenon.

00:12:30.614 --> 00:12:33.583
What do you mean
you saw dead people there?

00:12:42.726 --> 00:12:45.695
I'm, uh, Dr. Neria,

00:12:45.729 --> 00:12:49.563
the Chief Thanatologist
of this facility.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:52.899
Ensign Harry Kim of
the Federation Starship Voyager.

00:12:52.936 --> 00:12:56.269
I see.

00:12:56.306 --> 00:12:59.867
What race are you from?

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:02.208
We call ourselves human.

00:13:02.246 --> 00:13:04.908
We come from a planet
called Earth

00:13:04.948 --> 00:13:07.246
in a distant part of the galaxy.

00:13:07.284 --> 00:13:10.549
He said he saw dead
people on an asteroid.

00:13:10.587 --> 00:13:12.452
Dead?

00:13:12.489 --> 00:13:15.151
Look,
can you tell me where I am?

00:13:15.192 --> 00:13:18.218
Doctor, what does this mean?

00:13:18.262 --> 00:13:20.560
Rest, Hatil.

00:13:20.597 --> 00:13:22.963
There's no need for concern.

00:13:28.939 --> 00:13:32.602
May I speak to you
privately, Ensign Harry?

00:13:32.643 --> 00:13:35.373
Just Harry's fine.

00:13:35.412 --> 00:13:37.209
We are the Vhnori

00:13:37.247 --> 00:13:40.273
and this is our homeworld.

00:13:40.317 --> 00:13:42.911
We were investigating
one of the asteroids

00:13:42.953 --> 00:13:45.148
in the rings around your planet.

00:13:45.189 --> 00:13:47.885
There are no rings
around our world.

00:13:49.293 --> 00:13:51.784
So... the subspace vacuole

00:13:51.829 --> 00:13:54.559
must have transported me
somewhere else.

00:13:54.598 --> 00:13:57.726
Do you have any star charts
I could look at?

00:13:57.768 --> 00:14:00.293
I'd like to figure
out where I am now

00:14:00.337 --> 00:14:02.532
in relation to where I was.

00:14:02.573 --> 00:14:04.700
Where you are now

00:14:04.741 --> 00:14:07.039
is in the world of the living.

00:14:07.077 --> 00:14:09.170
Where you came from was...

00:14:10.681 --> 00:14:12.911
another dimension.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.281
Another dimension?

00:14:14.318 --> 00:14:15.307
Yes.

00:14:15.352 --> 00:14:18.947
You returned
from the Next Emanation.

00:14:19.022 --> 00:14:21.684
The afterlife.

00:14:28.432 --> 00:14:30.229
How were you able to revive her?

00:14:30.267 --> 00:14:32.701
It's a simple process,
really.

00:14:32.736 --> 00:14:34.636
She died of a cancerous growth
on the brain stem.

00:14:34.671 --> 00:14:37.868
I removed the tumor,
replicated new neural tissue,

00:14:37.908 --> 00:14:40.638
and used the standard
Starfleet postmortem

00:14:40.677 --> 00:14:42.372
resuscitation technique
for a Class-5 life-form.

00:14:42.412 --> 00:14:44.972
Why was she covered
with this bio-polymer?

00:14:45.082 --> 00:14:47.175
She wasn't covered
with it exactly.

00:14:47.217 --> 00:14:50.243
The bio-polymer is a byproduct
of her own tissues.

00:14:50.287 --> 00:14:51.254
Explain.

00:14:51.288 --> 00:14:52.653
As her tissues decayed,

00:14:52.689 --> 00:14:56.181
the cell membranes broke down
into a bio-polymer resin,

00:14:56.226 --> 00:14:58.854
which was then excreted
by her epidermal layer.

00:14:58.896 --> 00:15:01.865
My guess is it's
a natural decomposition process

00:15:01.899 --> 00:15:03.867
for this species.

00:15:03.901 --> 00:15:06.335
So the other bio-polymer fibers
we found in the cavern were...

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:07.337
Were probably the result

00:15:07.371 --> 00:15:09.498
of other bodies
that had decomposed

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:12.134
and left a residual membrane.

00:15:12.176 --> 00:15:13.370
In essence, Commander,

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:15.674
you were strolling
through dead bodies.

00:15:19.683 --> 00:15:20.945
Can you wake her?

00:15:21.051 --> 00:15:22.541
Yes, of course.

00:15:22.586 --> 00:15:25.350
Kes, 2cc's of netinaline.

00:15:37.834 --> 00:15:38.960
Hello.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.769
I know this must be

00:15:41.805 --> 00:15:44.399
very confusing for you,
but you're all right.

00:15:44.441 --> 00:15:47.171
My name is Kathryn Janeway.

00:15:47.211 --> 00:15:49.941
I'm Ptera.

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:52.141
Where's my brother?

00:15:52.182 --> 00:15:53.513
Your brother?

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.609
I'm afraid he's not here.

00:15:55.652 --> 00:15:58.280
But he's supposed to be here.

00:15:58.322 --> 00:16:00.790
They're all supposed to be here.

00:16:00.824 --> 00:16:03.452
Ptera, we were able
to remove the tumor

00:16:03.493 --> 00:16:04.482
from your brain.

00:16:04.528 --> 00:16:06.018
You're going to be all right.

00:16:06.063 --> 00:16:07.530
We revived you
because one of our...

00:16:07.564 --> 00:16:09.464
This is the Next Emanation?

00:16:09.499 --> 00:16:11.490
This is the afterlife?

00:16:14.271 --> 00:16:16.762
No. No, it's not.

00:16:16.807 --> 00:16:18.274
You're on a starship.

00:16:18.308 --> 00:16:19.866
This can't be right.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.275
My brother's supposed
to be here.

00:16:21.311 --> 00:16:22.300
Something's wrong.

00:16:22.346 --> 00:16:24.143
- Let me explain.
- No.

00:16:24.181 --> 00:16:26.513
No, get away from me.

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.539
This isn't right!

00:16:27.584 --> 00:16:28.573
This can't be right!

00:16:40.631 --> 00:16:42.462
You're saying there
was a woman in here

00:16:42.499 --> 00:16:43.557
just before I arrived?

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.624
That's right.

00:16:44.668 --> 00:16:45.760
Her name was Ptera.

00:16:45.802 --> 00:16:49.533
She was dying of a tumorous
lesion to her midbrain.

00:16:49.573 --> 00:16:50.972
Dying?

00:16:51.074 --> 00:16:52.837
So she wasn't dead yet?

00:16:52.876 --> 00:16:54.503
No, of course not.

00:16:54.544 --> 00:16:57.479
She didn't die until
the cenotaph was activated.

00:16:57.514 --> 00:16:59.744
That's the purpose
of the cenotaph...

00:16:59.783 --> 00:17:01.614
it terminates a person's life

00:17:01.652 --> 00:17:04.746
just before the appearance
of a spectral rupture,

00:17:04.788 --> 00:17:06.688
and then it allows their body

00:17:06.723 --> 00:17:09.021
to be taken
to the Next Emanation.

00:17:09.059 --> 00:17:10.686
Spectral rupture.

00:17:10.727 --> 00:17:13.355
Well... I can show you.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:20.169
This looks like what we would
call a subspace vacuole.

00:17:20.203 --> 00:17:22.694
Does the cenotaph
create these ruptures?

00:17:22.739 --> 00:17:24.866
No. They're
natural occurrences...

00:17:24.908 --> 00:17:25.875
once every six hours.

00:17:25.909 --> 00:17:27.706
This entire complex
was built on this site

00:17:27.744 --> 00:17:29.473
because a spectral rupture
occurs here.

00:17:29.513 --> 00:17:32.573
We have thousands
of such sites on our world.

00:17:32.616 --> 00:17:37.519
Forgive my curiosity,
Harry, but, uh,

00:17:37.554 --> 00:17:39.385
you are the first person

00:17:39.423 --> 00:17:43.325
ever to come back
from the afterlife.

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:45.692
I have quite a few questions.

00:17:45.729 --> 00:17:49.961
You said
that you saw dead bodies?

00:17:50.033 --> 00:17:51.500
That's right.

00:17:51.535 --> 00:17:56.529
There were...
seven females, 11 males.

00:17:56.573 --> 00:17:58.302
Some of the bodies
had been there for years.

00:17:58.342 --> 00:17:59.969
Others just for a few days.

00:18:00.043 --> 00:18:02.102
Are you saying that when we die,

00:18:02.145 --> 00:18:06.844
we go to some asteroid
and decompose?

00:18:07.884 --> 00:18:09.374
Well...

00:18:09.419 --> 00:18:11.148
that's what
it looked like to us.

00:18:11.188 --> 00:18:13.588
These bodies,
did you perform

00:18:13.623 --> 00:18:15.557
any kind of bio-scans on them?

00:18:15.592 --> 00:18:17.150
W-Was there any specific

00:18:17.194 --> 00:18:19.128
medical data
that you can remember?

00:18:19.162 --> 00:18:21.926
Doctor, maybe I should
just stop right there.

00:18:21.998 --> 00:18:25.365
This is what my people call
a First Contact situation,

00:18:25.402 --> 00:18:27.802
and we've learned
to be very careful

00:18:27.838 --> 00:18:31.467
about how much we tell
alien cultures we've just met.

00:18:31.508 --> 00:18:33.806
I would like to start
a complete bioanalysis

00:18:33.844 --> 00:18:35.004
as soon as possible.

00:18:35.045 --> 00:18:36.245
If you'll just follow
Dr. Ranora.

00:18:36.245 --> 00:18:38.941
If you'll just follow
Dr. Ranora.

00:18:38.981 --> 00:18:40.448
Bioanalysis?

00:18:40.482 --> 00:18:43.849
Look, all I want to do
is get back to my ship

00:18:43.885 --> 00:18:46.718
and I think there might be a way
to use this spectral

00:18:46.755 --> 00:18:47.722
rupture of yours to...

00:18:47.756 --> 00:18:49.781
You're not going anywhere.

00:18:49.825 --> 00:18:55.957
You are our first glimpse
into what lies beyond death.

00:18:56.064 --> 00:19:00.262
We are not going to let
this opportunity pass us by.

00:19:02.838 --> 00:19:05.830
We've completed our analysis
of the ring system.

00:19:05.874 --> 00:19:08.536
Our sensors have detected
over 200,000 alien bodies

00:19:08.577 --> 00:19:10.374
on various asteroids
in the rings.

00:19:10.412 --> 00:19:11.504
From what we can tell,

00:19:11.546 --> 00:19:14.174
a subspace vacuole appears
about every two hours,

00:19:14.216 --> 00:19:16.343
deposits a body,
and then disappears.

00:19:16.385 --> 00:19:18.216
We need to focus
on those vacuoles.

00:19:18.253 --> 00:19:20.084
Concentrate on trying
to probe them

00:19:20.122 --> 00:19:22.113
with a high-resolution
subspace scan.

00:19:22.157 --> 00:19:23.522
See if you can find
any sign of Mr. Kim.

00:19:23.558 --> 00:19:25.355
Sick Bay to Captain Janeway.

00:19:25.394 --> 00:19:26.361
Go ahead.

00:19:26.395 --> 00:19:28.260
Our guest
has regained consciousness

00:19:28.297 --> 00:19:29.855
and she's a little calmer
this time.

00:19:29.898 --> 00:19:31.991
I'm on my way.
You have the Bridge.

00:19:34.503 --> 00:19:36.095
That's, that's all I know.

00:19:36.138 --> 00:19:38.698
I'm sorry. I can't
tell you anything more.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.731
You've told me quite a bit.

00:19:40.776 --> 00:19:42.869
At least now I have an idea

00:19:42.911 --> 00:19:45.709
of what might
have happened to Mr. Kim.

00:19:45.747 --> 00:19:48.181
Is there anything
I can do for you?

00:19:48.216 --> 00:19:50.946
Well, I'd, I'd like
some answers.

00:19:50.986 --> 00:19:52.613
About what?

00:19:52.654 --> 00:19:55.088
About what happens
to my people when we die.

00:19:57.092 --> 00:20:00.391
We're not sure, exactly,

00:20:00.429 --> 00:20:04.889
but from what we do know,
the vacuoles deposit the bodies

00:20:04.933 --> 00:20:07.299
on the asteroids
in this ring system.

00:20:07.336 --> 00:20:08.769
And then what?

00:20:08.804 --> 00:20:10.203
I'm not sure what you mean.

00:20:10.238 --> 00:20:11.967
We're supposed to evolve

00:20:12.007 --> 00:20:15.170
into a higher level
of consciousness when we die.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:16.199
We're supposed to gain

00:20:16.244 --> 00:20:18.075
a greater understanding
of the universe.

00:20:18.113 --> 00:20:21.674
All of our questions
are supposed to be answered.

00:20:21.717 --> 00:20:24.686
Ptera, I know this
must be frightening for you.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.950
You've been through
a very traumatic experience...

00:20:26.988 --> 00:20:29.422
it would frighten me...

00:20:29.458 --> 00:20:31.858
but please try to understand,

00:20:31.893 --> 00:20:35.420
just because I don't have
the answers to your questions

00:20:35.464 --> 00:20:36.795
doesn't mean there aren't any.

00:20:39.468 --> 00:20:42.232
My brother...

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:45.000
I always thought
I'd see him again.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:51.001
I had so many things to tell him
about his children...

00:20:51.079 --> 00:20:53.070
the people he left behind...

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.275
but he isn't here, is he?

00:20:57.319 --> 00:20:59.810
He's...

00:21:01.223 --> 00:21:05.125
So, what am I supposed
to do now,

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.755
spend the rest of my life
on this... this... starship?

00:21:08.797 --> 00:21:13.257
Ptera, I am going to do
everything in my power

00:21:13.301 --> 00:21:15.861
to figure out
just how you got here,

00:21:15.904 --> 00:21:19.499
and as soon as I know anything,
I will tell you.

00:21:19.541 --> 00:21:22.237
All right?

00:21:22.277 --> 00:21:23.767
All right.

00:21:23.812 --> 00:21:25.939
Maybe we should
get out of Sick Bay.

00:21:25.981 --> 00:21:28.279
Let you walk around
for a while, clear your mind.

00:21:28.316 --> 00:21:30.216
Maybe get something to eat.

00:21:30.252 --> 00:21:31.549
Are you hungry?

00:21:31.586 --> 00:21:34.885
Yes. Actually, I could use
something to eat.

00:21:35.891 --> 00:21:36.858
What was that?!

00:21:36.892 --> 00:21:38.382
Janeway to Bridge.
Report.

00:21:38.427 --> 00:21:40.292
There's some kind
of dimensional distortion

00:21:40.328 --> 00:21:42.159
forming near Main Engineering,
Captain.

00:21:42.197 --> 00:21:44.358
It looks like
a subspace vacuole.

00:21:44.399 --> 00:21:46.526
Janeway to Engineering.
B'Elanna, what's going on?

00:21:46.568 --> 00:21:49.196
I've pinpointed the location,
Captain.

00:21:49.237 --> 00:21:51.364
It's right here in Engineering.

00:21:51.406 --> 00:21:53.067
Stand by.

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:04.084
Hatil, what are you saying?

00:22:07.055 --> 00:22:10.957
I'm just not sure I'm ready,
that's all.

00:22:11.059 --> 00:22:13.857
I don't understand.

00:22:13.895 --> 00:22:16.728
Neither do I.

00:22:16.765 --> 00:22:19.928
It's just
that I'm starting to wonder

00:22:19.968 --> 00:22:23.699
what really happens
when we die...

00:22:23.738 --> 00:22:25.638
if I'm really going on

00:22:25.674 --> 00:22:29.701
to a higher level
of consciousness.

00:22:29.744 --> 00:22:32.804
The alien, what has
he been telling you?

00:22:32.848 --> 00:22:35.874
All he's done is made
me stop and think

00:22:35.917 --> 00:22:38.385
about something we've
always taken for granted.

00:22:39.921 --> 00:22:42.822
And now that I've
thought about it,

00:22:42.858 --> 00:22:45.759
I'm not so eager to go
through with it anymore.

00:22:45.794 --> 00:22:48.729
Hatil, we know
nothing about him,

00:22:48.763 --> 00:22:52.597
or why he's come here,
or why he's spreading lies

00:22:52.634 --> 00:22:53.999
about the Next Emanation.

00:22:54.102 --> 00:22:56.536
All I know is
you can't throw away

00:22:56.571 --> 00:22:58.903
a lifetime of belief
because of him.

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:00.931
It doesn't make any sense.

00:23:02.711 --> 00:23:05.737
I don't know
what to think anymore.

00:23:07.249 --> 00:23:09.114
I'm scared, Araya.

00:23:11.119 --> 00:23:13.519
It's going to be all right.

00:23:13.555 --> 00:23:16.388
Think about your father.

00:23:16.424 --> 00:23:18.187
He's waiting for you.

00:23:24.266 --> 00:23:27.497
I'll see you
at the Transference Ritual.

00:23:32.908 --> 00:23:35.706
I don't know who you are,
or where you come from,

00:23:35.744 --> 00:23:38.076
but you stay away
from my husband.

00:23:38.113 --> 00:23:40.240
I'm sorry.

00:23:40.282 --> 00:23:41.977
I didn't mean to...

00:23:44.586 --> 00:23:48.113
Harry,
you have to forgive my wife.

00:23:48.156 --> 00:23:52.092
She's having trouble
understanding my concerns

00:23:52.127 --> 00:23:53.958
about the afterlife.

00:23:55.096 --> 00:23:56.825
That's why I'm here.

00:23:56.865 --> 00:23:59.356
I'm, uh...

00:23:59.401 --> 00:24:01.266
getting ready to die.

00:24:01.303 --> 00:24:06.707
Forgive me for asking again,
but can you tell me anything

00:24:06.741 --> 00:24:09.835
about what I might find
in the Next Emanation?

00:24:09.878 --> 00:24:11.846
Everyone keeps asking me that,

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:14.713
and I just keep giving
the same answer.

00:24:14.749 --> 00:24:15.943
I don't know.

00:24:16.051 --> 00:24:20.147
But you do come
from the afterlife.

00:24:20.188 --> 00:24:23.680
I come from a different reality,
maybe another dimension,

00:24:23.725 --> 00:24:26.193
and maybe it is your afterlife.

00:24:26.227 --> 00:24:27.717
I don't know.

00:24:27.762 --> 00:24:30.890
All I do know is that there
are countless billions

00:24:30.932 --> 00:24:33.526
of people there
who are born, live and die

00:24:33.568 --> 00:24:34.535
just like you do here.

00:24:34.569 --> 00:24:38.369
But you did see my people there.

00:24:38.406 --> 00:24:40.237
You said they were dead.

00:24:40.275 --> 00:24:43.574
Yes, but...

00:24:43.612 --> 00:24:47.412
Look, for all I know,
your thanatologists are right,

00:24:47.449 --> 00:24:48.746
and all I saw were

00:24:48.783 --> 00:24:50.910
the corporeal remains
of your people,

00:24:50.952 --> 00:24:53.887
and you do go on
to a higher consciousness.

00:24:53.922 --> 00:24:55.617
But it's, uh...

00:24:55.657 --> 00:24:59.650
it's also possible that...

00:24:59.694 --> 00:25:02.822
there is no higher
existence for us...

00:25:02.864 --> 00:25:07.927
that when we die,
we simply cease to exist.

00:25:08.036 --> 00:25:10.664
I...

00:25:10.705 --> 00:25:13.299
I really can't say.

00:25:13.341 --> 00:25:16.936
I don't know what happens
to your people after they die.

00:25:17.012 --> 00:25:20.038
I don't even know what happens
to my people after they die.

00:25:20.081 --> 00:25:24.677
Don't you have thanatologists,
people who study death?

00:25:24.719 --> 00:25:26.949
Well, sort of.

00:25:27.055 --> 00:25:30.616
There have certainly been
medical experts,

00:25:30.659 --> 00:25:32.684
philosophers, theologians,

00:25:32.727 --> 00:25:35.719
who have spent
a great deal of time

00:25:35.764 --> 00:25:37.891
debating what happens
after death,

00:25:37.932 --> 00:25:40.526
but no one's come up
with an answer yet.

00:25:40.568 --> 00:25:43.833
My people have come
to think of death

00:25:43.872 --> 00:25:47.330
as just another stage
of our existence.

00:25:47.375 --> 00:25:51.345
There are some people
who are even eager to die.

00:25:51.478 --> 00:25:55.471
If they feel depressed
or lonely in this life,

00:25:55.515 --> 00:25:57.881
they simply move on
to the next one.

00:25:57.918 --> 00:25:59.385
Is that why you're here?

00:25:59.419 --> 00:26:01.887
Because you're not happy
with your life?

00:26:05.959 --> 00:26:08.450
Ever since the, um...

00:26:08.495 --> 00:26:09.894
accident...

00:26:12.466 --> 00:26:15.629
life hasn't been easy.

00:26:17.137 --> 00:26:20.664
But I have to say this
is more my family's idea

00:26:20.707 --> 00:26:22.038
than it is mine.

00:26:22.075 --> 00:26:23.099
Your family.

00:26:23.143 --> 00:26:26.476
I'm a burden to them right now.

00:26:26.513 --> 00:26:30.540
It takes a lot of their time
and resources to care for me,

00:26:30.584 --> 00:26:33.917
and I can't give
much back to them.

00:26:33.954 --> 00:26:38.391
So there was a family meeting,
and it was agreed that...

00:26:38.425 --> 00:26:41.588
I should move on
to the Next Emanation.

00:26:46.600 --> 00:26:48.227
You look appalled.

00:26:48.268 --> 00:26:50.896
It's not my place
to judge your culture,

00:26:50.937 --> 00:26:52.802
but from my perspective,

00:26:52.839 --> 00:26:55.467
it's a little chilling
to hear that.

00:26:57.344 --> 00:27:01.610
Even though the family
did it out of... love...

00:27:03.083 --> 00:27:09.420
and everyone was happy for me,
and they said they'd see me

00:27:09.456 --> 00:27:11.981
when they got
to the Next Emanation...

00:27:13.860 --> 00:27:16.192
I have to admit,

00:27:16.229 --> 00:27:17.628
there is a little voice
inside of me

00:27:17.664 --> 00:27:20.428
that is terrified of dying

00:27:20.467 --> 00:27:22.298
and since
I've been talking to you...

00:27:23.804 --> 00:27:26.102
that little voice
has started to get...

00:27:26.139 --> 00:27:28.039
Iouder.

00:27:37.551 --> 00:27:39.746
I'm reading another vacuole
forming on the ship.

00:27:39.786 --> 00:27:41.754
Tuvok, try remodulating
the shield harmonics.

00:27:41.788 --> 00:27:42.914
It's no use, Captain.

00:27:42.956 --> 00:27:45.754
The vacuole is still forming.

00:27:53.500 --> 00:27:55.297
Take the body
to the ship's morgue.

00:28:00.207 --> 00:28:02.471
This is odd.

00:28:02.509 --> 00:28:03.703
Three bodies have appeared

00:28:03.743 --> 00:28:05.904
on Voyager so far,
and each one of them

00:28:05.979 --> 00:28:09.005
has released some kind
of neural energy.

00:28:09.049 --> 00:28:10.641
In every case,
the energy has passed

00:28:10.684 --> 00:28:14.814
through the hull
and out into the rings.

00:28:14.855 --> 00:28:17.255
The energy's frequency
is identical

00:28:17.290 --> 00:28:20.157
to the ambient radiation
in the asteroid field.

00:28:22.395 --> 00:28:23.726
The vacuoles are disrupting

00:28:23.763 --> 00:28:25.526
the warp core's
magnetic interlocks.

00:28:25.565 --> 00:28:27.931
It won't be long before
we lose antimatter containment.

00:28:28.001 --> 00:28:29.161
The vacuoles have all formed

00:28:29.202 --> 00:28:31.466
within 20 meters
of the warp core.

00:28:31.505 --> 00:28:33.496
They might be attracted to it.

00:28:33.540 --> 00:28:34.939
Janeway to Bridge.

00:28:35.041 --> 00:28:36.338
Mr. Paris, lay in a course.

00:28:36.376 --> 00:28:37.468
I want to get at least

00:28:37.511 --> 00:28:39.877
a half a light year away.
Warp seven.

00:28:39.913 --> 00:28:41.380
Aye, Captain.

00:28:48.421 --> 00:28:49.854
Paris to Janeway.

00:28:49.890 --> 00:28:51.858
I've brought us out of warp.

00:28:51.892 --> 00:28:54.725
We're point six light-years
from the ring system.

00:28:54.761 --> 00:28:57.423
Any other subspace
vacuoles forming?

00:28:57.464 --> 00:28:58.761
No.

00:28:58.798 --> 00:29:00.288
The magnetic interlocks
have stabilized.

00:29:00.333 --> 00:29:01.391
I think we're safe out here.

00:29:01.434 --> 00:29:03.368
Begin working
on a way to protect

00:29:03.403 --> 00:29:04.529
the warp core
from these vacuoles.

00:29:04.571 --> 00:29:05.663
Aye, Captain.

00:29:11.011 --> 00:29:14.777
Sometimes I come in here and
just stare out at the stars.

00:29:14.814 --> 00:29:15.872
For hours.

00:29:15.916 --> 00:29:18.908
I never get tired
of looking at them.

00:29:18.952 --> 00:29:21.887
We were always told we
would see beautiful sights

00:29:21.922 --> 00:29:25.517
in the Next Emanation...
colors, lights...

00:29:25.559 --> 00:29:27.652
and that we would see
them with new eyes

00:29:27.694 --> 00:29:28.854
and a new understanding.

00:29:28.895 --> 00:29:32.456
But now...

00:29:32.499 --> 00:29:35.696
what happened to the others...

00:29:35.735 --> 00:29:38.135
my brother...

00:29:38.171 --> 00:29:39.695
my father...

00:29:39.739 --> 00:29:43.607
and everyone before them.

00:29:43.643 --> 00:29:47.101
People die every day
on my world.

00:29:47.147 --> 00:29:50.275
Do they all end up
as lifeless corpses?

00:29:50.317 --> 00:29:54.413
When people die on my world,
we bury them beneath the soil

00:29:54.454 --> 00:29:58.720
and we believe that their comra
is released into the afterlife.

00:29:58.758 --> 00:30:00.919
Their comra?

00:30:00.961 --> 00:30:02.929
Our soul, our spirit,

00:30:02.963 --> 00:30:05.124
the essence of our beings.

00:30:05.165 --> 00:30:07.633
Maybe something similar
happens to you.

00:30:09.135 --> 00:30:12.127
But you don't understand.

00:30:12.172 --> 00:30:15.608
We don't believe
in any kind of spirit.

00:30:15.642 --> 00:30:19.635
When we die, we're supposed
to reappear as physical beings

00:30:19.679 --> 00:30:21.647
with arms and legs.

00:30:21.681 --> 00:30:23.342
That's the whole point

00:30:23.383 --> 00:30:26.750
of sending our people
through the spectral ruptures.

00:30:26.786 --> 00:30:31.314
We're supposed to travel on to
the Next Emanation as ourselves,

00:30:31.358 --> 00:30:33.792
and be reunited
with our families.

00:30:37.998 --> 00:30:40.398
But none of that is true...

00:30:40.433 --> 00:30:41.991
is it?

00:30:47.040 --> 00:30:50.032
None of the people I love
are here.

00:30:51.611 --> 00:30:53.169
I'm alone.

00:30:57.117 --> 00:30:58.982
I don't belong here.

00:30:59.019 --> 00:31:01.351
I can't live like this.

00:31:01.388 --> 00:31:04.482
Please, can't you send me home?

00:31:04.524 --> 00:31:07.493
I think there is
only one person on this ship

00:31:07.527 --> 00:31:10.189
who could answer that question.

00:31:10.230 --> 00:31:13.597
We're doing everything we can
to get you back home, Ptera.

00:31:13.633 --> 00:31:15.863
Once we locate
our missing officer,

00:31:15.902 --> 00:31:17.870
we're hoping he might be able
to tell us enough to...

00:31:17.904 --> 00:31:18.871
Wait a minute, Captain.

00:31:18.905 --> 00:31:21.430
Maybe there is a way
to send Ptera home

00:31:21.474 --> 00:31:23.874
and find Ensign Kim
at the same time.

00:31:23.910 --> 00:31:25.343
Explain.

00:31:25.378 --> 00:31:27.938
What if we recreated
the transporter accident?

00:31:27.981 --> 00:31:29.778
If it's true that Harry was
pulled through the vacuole

00:31:29.816 --> 00:31:31.283
during transport,
we might be able

00:31:31.317 --> 00:31:33.376
to reproduce
those circumstances,

00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:34.717
and send Ptera home.

00:31:34.754 --> 00:31:37.518
We could send Ptera through
with a subspace transponder,

00:31:37.557 --> 00:31:38.819
and hope the signal
will penetrate

00:31:38.858 --> 00:31:39.825
the dimensional barrier,

00:31:39.859 --> 00:31:41.656
and allow us
to lock on to Kim

00:31:41.695 --> 00:31:42.662
with a transporter beam.

00:31:42.696 --> 00:31:43.663
Right.

00:31:43.697 --> 00:31:44.925
So I can get home?

00:31:46.099 --> 00:31:48.124
Ptera, you should know

00:31:48.168 --> 00:31:50.329
that there's no guarantee
this is going to work.

00:31:50.370 --> 00:31:51.962
I understand the risk,

00:31:52.005 --> 00:31:53.996
but I've already
been dead once,

00:31:54.074 --> 00:31:57.009
and I'm prepared to die again
if necessary.

00:31:57.077 --> 00:31:59.944
So if there's a chance
I can get home,

00:31:59.979 --> 00:32:01.606
I'm willing to take the risk.

00:32:01.648 --> 00:32:04.378
All right.

00:32:04.417 --> 00:32:06.385
Commander, prepare
a subspace transponder

00:32:06.419 --> 00:32:07.852
and teach Ptera how to use it.

00:32:07.887 --> 00:32:09.047
Aye, Captain.

00:32:11.624 --> 00:32:13.558
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:32:13.593 --> 00:32:15.720
We've returned
to the ring system,

00:32:15.762 --> 00:32:18.890
and we're preparing to send
Ptera back to her dimension.

00:32:18.932 --> 00:32:20.593
Lieutenant Torres
has found a way

00:32:20.633 --> 00:32:23.124
to temporarily protect the
warp core against the vacuoles,

00:32:23.169 --> 00:32:24.431
but she is uncertain

00:32:24.471 --> 00:32:28.168
how long her measures
will be effective.

00:32:28.208 --> 00:32:30.972
You understand the instructions
for Mr. Kim, if you find him?

00:32:31.010 --> 00:32:32.204
Yes.

00:32:32.245 --> 00:32:33.234
We've got one, Commander,

00:32:33.279 --> 00:32:35.611
forming ten meters
below us, Deck 13.

00:32:35.648 --> 00:32:36.945
Okay, let's see
if your dampening field

00:32:36.983 --> 00:32:39.315
is going to protect
the warp core.

00:32:39.352 --> 00:32:43.550
The field is fluctuating
slightly... but holding.

00:32:43.590 --> 00:32:45.615
Engineering
to Transporter Room 3.

00:32:45.658 --> 00:32:47.319
There's a vacuole
forming on Deck 13.

00:32:47.360 --> 00:32:49.294
Magnetic interlocks are stable.

00:32:49.329 --> 00:32:50.455
Acknowledged.

00:32:50.497 --> 00:32:52.932
I see the vacuole.
Locking on.

00:32:59.672 --> 00:33:01.537
Good luck, Ptera.

00:33:03.008 --> 00:33:04.942
I have a transporter lock.

00:33:05.044 --> 00:33:06.341
Energizing.

00:33:06.378 --> 00:33:09.905
Matching her pattern
to the subspace distortions.

00:33:09.949 --> 00:33:12.440
Wait a minute, the vacuole
is shutting down.

00:33:12.484 --> 00:33:14.884
I can't get her pattern through.

00:33:14.920 --> 00:33:16.512
Abort the procedure.
Pull her back.

00:33:16.555 --> 00:33:19.615
I'm trying.
I'm losing her pattern.

00:33:19.658 --> 00:33:21.785
Shunt emergency power
into buffer tank 4.

00:33:23.462 --> 00:33:26.192
That's it.
I've got the pattern.

00:33:37.810 --> 00:33:39.334
She's dead.

00:33:39.378 --> 00:33:40.367
Is there any brain activity?

00:33:40.412 --> 00:33:41.538
Can we revive her?

00:33:43.749 --> 00:33:44.716
Janeway to Lieutenant Torres.

00:33:44.750 --> 00:33:46.809
How long until we have to leave?

00:33:46.852 --> 00:33:48.843
I'd say we're safe
for another two hours.

00:33:48.887 --> 00:33:50.912
That gives us two hours
to find Mr. Kim.

00:33:50.956 --> 00:33:53.151
We'll have to stay within
high-range scanner range.

00:33:53.192 --> 00:33:54.557
Perform another subspace scan.

00:33:54.593 --> 00:33:56.925
This time, extend
the scan radius to ten AU.

00:33:56.962 --> 00:33:58.759
I'm on my way to Engineering.
Janeway out.

00:33:58.797 --> 00:33:59.764
Aye, Captain.

00:33:59.798 --> 00:34:02.392
Ensign, beam her onto
one of the asteroids.

00:34:02.434 --> 00:34:03.924
Aye, Captain.

00:34:04.003 --> 00:34:05.834
That's where
she was meant to be.

00:34:11.777 --> 00:34:14.837
I hope you find
your afterlife, Ptera.

00:34:18.517 --> 00:34:19.643
Why?

00:34:19.685 --> 00:34:21.949
We want to make
a more detailed scan

00:34:21.987 --> 00:34:23.511
of your
microcellular structures,

00:34:23.555 --> 00:34:25.955
and a complete examination
of your neural chemistry.

00:34:26.058 --> 00:34:29.459
This facility isn't equipped
for such a detailed bioanalysis.

00:34:29.495 --> 00:34:32.896
The complex at Paffran
has everything we need.

00:34:32.931 --> 00:34:35.923
Look, if my ship
is still searching for me,

00:34:35.968 --> 00:34:37.868
they're not going
to stay there forever.

00:34:37.903 --> 00:34:39.063
I have to get back.

00:34:39.104 --> 00:34:40.401
That's not possible.

00:34:40.439 --> 00:34:43.340
We don't even understand
how you got here.

00:34:43.375 --> 00:34:45.343
Then maybe I can figure out
a way to get back.

00:34:45.377 --> 00:34:47.311
Let me take a look
at one of those cenotaphs.

00:34:47.346 --> 00:34:48.836
There's no time for that.

00:34:48.881 --> 00:34:51.281
Word about you has spread
very quickly, Harry.

00:34:51.316 --> 00:34:53.375
Not only in the scientific
world, but in the community

00:34:53.419 --> 00:34:54.386
at large.

00:34:54.420 --> 00:34:58.379
There are many people
who are very... nervous

00:34:58.424 --> 00:34:59.982
about what you represent.

00:35:00.059 --> 00:35:01.356
Some even see you as a threat

00:35:01.393 --> 00:35:03.156
to their beliefs
about the afterlife.

00:35:03.195 --> 00:35:07.063
We need to take you
to a more secure location.

00:35:07.099 --> 00:35:09.567
It's for your own protection.

00:35:09.601 --> 00:35:11.296
Wait!

00:35:11.336 --> 00:35:13.827
I'm sorry, Harry.

00:35:13.872 --> 00:35:15.863
It's out of my control.

00:35:25.451 --> 00:35:27.180
What are you doing?

00:35:27.219 --> 00:35:30.086
Preparing for
the Transference Ritual.

00:35:32.124 --> 00:35:34.888
This is a ceremonial shroud

00:35:34.927 --> 00:35:39.159
that's been in my family
for five generations.

00:35:39.198 --> 00:35:44.659
So they make you wrap yourself
in your own death shroud.

00:35:44.703 --> 00:35:48.503
It's something we look
forward to, actually.

00:35:48.540 --> 00:35:51.976
I remember
when my father used this shroud,

00:35:52.077 --> 00:35:55.979
and his father before him.

00:35:56.081 --> 00:35:59.983
The difference is,
when my father put this on,

00:36:00.085 --> 00:36:05.421
there was no doubt in his mind
about where he was going.

00:36:05.457 --> 00:36:07.425
Can't you just back out?

00:36:07.459 --> 00:36:09.450
Say you've changed your mind?

00:36:09.495 --> 00:36:16.298
I... have thought of just
walking out and disappearing.

00:36:16.335 --> 00:36:19.304
I have some friends
in the Cararian Mountains.

00:36:19.338 --> 00:36:23.138
They would be willing
to let me stay with them.

00:36:23.175 --> 00:36:26.144
But my family
would worry about me.

00:36:26.178 --> 00:36:29.147
They'd wonder
what was happening,

00:36:29.181 --> 00:36:35.711
if I was all right,
if I were hurt...

00:36:35.754 --> 00:36:39.315
No. Everyone's expecting
a Transference Ritual

00:36:39.358 --> 00:36:41.792
and I'm going to give them one.

00:36:41.827 --> 00:36:46.264
What if you did disappear
into the mountains,

00:36:46.298 --> 00:36:49.267
but your family
thought you were dead?

00:36:49.301 --> 00:36:52.464
I mean, they're here for
a Transference Ritual, right?

00:36:52.504 --> 00:36:56.531
Do you realize
what you're suggesting?

00:36:56.575 --> 00:36:57.974
It's perfect.

00:36:58.076 --> 00:37:01.375
Those cenotaphs send your people
back to my dimension,

00:37:01.413 --> 00:37:03.540
which is where I want to go.

00:37:03.582 --> 00:37:07.712
Voyager's probably still near
the asteroid searching for me.

00:37:07.753 --> 00:37:09.550
As soon as I appear,

00:37:09.588 --> 00:37:12.648
they'll pick up my signal
and beam me aboard.

00:37:12.691 --> 00:37:14.158
And you...

00:37:14.193 --> 00:37:16.661
you can just disappear.

00:37:16.695 --> 00:37:19.163
Your family will
think you're dead,

00:37:19.198 --> 00:37:23.760
and you can live out your life
in the mountains.

00:37:23.802 --> 00:37:27.932
Harry, if you go
into that cenotaph

00:37:28.006 --> 00:37:29.940
and go through
with the Transference Ritual,

00:37:30.042 --> 00:37:31.600
you'll die.

00:37:31.643 --> 00:37:35.101
Well, if Voyager can
beam me aboard quickly enough,

00:37:35.147 --> 00:37:37.911
our doctor should be able
to revive me.

00:37:39.585 --> 00:37:42.952
Medicine's pretty advanced
in our culture.

00:37:43.055 --> 00:37:45.250
I've heard of cases where people
have been dead for hours

00:37:45.290 --> 00:37:46.848
and still been
brought back to life.

00:37:48.293 --> 00:37:49.954
But it's not certain.

00:37:50.028 --> 00:37:54.089
No, it's not...

00:37:54.132 --> 00:37:58.125
but I think this
is my only chance to get home.

00:38:06.410 --> 00:38:09.243
The shroud has to be wrapped
in a particular way.

00:38:09.279 --> 00:38:11.008
I'll show you how.

00:38:11.048 --> 00:38:13.016
But we have to hurry.

00:38:13.050 --> 00:38:16.679
I'm scheduled for Transference
in less than an hour.

00:38:22.226 --> 00:38:24.694
A pleasant trip, Hatil.

00:38:24.728 --> 00:38:27.697
Say hello to Varel and Toyan.

00:38:27.731 --> 00:38:30.723
I'll see you there
in a few years.

00:38:32.770 --> 00:38:34.931
We are joined here today

00:38:34.972 --> 00:38:38.738
to bid farewell
to our dear friend Hatil Garan.

00:38:38.776 --> 00:38:41.336
We salute not only his life,

00:38:41.378 --> 00:38:44.677
but the manner in which
he has chosen to end it.

00:38:44.715 --> 00:38:47.684
He makes
a noble sacrifice today,

00:38:47.718 --> 00:38:51.210
that his family
may have a better tomorrow.

00:38:51.255 --> 00:38:54.224
We prepare to send him on
to the Next Emanation

00:38:54.258 --> 00:38:56.624
with the full knowledge
and faith

00:38:56.660 --> 00:39:01.097
that the life he will find there
is better than the one here,

00:39:01.131 --> 00:39:04.862
that he will no longer
be hampered by his infirmities,

00:39:04.902 --> 00:39:08.303
and that he will come
to understand the cosmos

00:39:08.338 --> 00:39:11.330
in a way that he could
never have imagined.

00:39:14.178 --> 00:39:17.477
Good-bye, Hatil.

00:39:17.514 --> 00:39:19.846
I love you.

00:39:43.073 --> 00:39:45.200
Another vacuole.
Deck 15.

00:39:45.242 --> 00:39:48.678
The body of an alien female
has been left behind.

00:39:48.712 --> 00:39:50.873
Chakotay
to Transporter Room 3.

00:39:50.914 --> 00:39:52.814
Lock on to the body on Deck 15,

00:39:52.850 --> 00:39:54.841
and transport it
to one of the asteroids.

00:39:54.885 --> 00:39:56.113
Aye, sir.

00:39:56.153 --> 00:39:57.950
Status on the warp core,
Lieutenant.

00:39:58.021 --> 00:40:00.489
The dampening field's
down to 21 percent.

00:40:00.524 --> 00:40:02.515
The interlocks won't
hold much longer.

00:40:04.161 --> 00:40:06.459
I recommend leaving, Captain.

00:40:15.806 --> 00:40:17.433
Very well.

00:40:17.474 --> 00:40:19.806
Mr. Paris, bring us about.

00:40:19.843 --> 00:40:21.834
Prepare to resume our...

00:40:22.846 --> 00:40:24.973
Captain,
I'm picking up a vacuole

00:40:25.015 --> 00:40:26.312
forming on Deck 12.

00:40:26.350 --> 00:40:28.477
It deposited a human body...

00:40:28.519 --> 00:40:29.986
Human?

00:40:30.020 --> 00:40:31.851
But it's dead.

00:40:33.524 --> 00:40:34.491
Janeway to Seska.

00:40:34.525 --> 00:40:35.492
There's a body on Deck 12.

00:40:35.526 --> 00:40:36.993
Beam it directly to Sick Bay.

00:40:37.027 --> 00:40:38.358
Yes, Captain.

00:40:43.800 --> 00:40:46.291
2cc's cordrazine.

00:41:07.124 --> 00:41:10.218
Relax, Mr. Kim.
Everything's fine.

00:41:10.260 --> 00:41:12.285
You're alive.

00:41:44.928 --> 00:41:46.555
Mind if I join you?

00:41:46.597 --> 00:41:48.565
No, not at all.
Please.

00:41:48.599 --> 00:41:49.930
Thank you.

00:41:52.436 --> 00:41:54.961
So, how are you feeling?

00:41:55.005 --> 00:41:58.304
Better. I'll be ready
for duty tomorrow morning.

00:41:58.342 --> 00:42:00.936
You're off duty
for the next two days.

00:42:00.978 --> 00:42:02.445
Captain, I'm fine.

00:42:02.479 --> 00:42:05.573
It's not a reflection
on your capabilities, Ensign.

00:42:05.616 --> 00:42:10.576
I just want to give you a chance
to reflect on what's happened.

00:42:10.621 --> 00:42:13.283
This may not make
much sense to you now...

00:42:13.323 --> 00:42:16.292
a young man
at the beginning of his career...

00:42:16.326 --> 00:42:18.419
but one of the things you learn
as you move up the ranks

00:42:18.462 --> 00:42:22.398
and get a little older
is that...

00:42:22.432 --> 00:42:26.459
you wish you had more time
in your youth to really...

00:42:26.503 --> 00:42:29.233
absorb all the things
that happen to you.

00:42:29.272 --> 00:42:31.934
It goes by so fast.

00:42:33.443 --> 00:42:36.241
It's so easy to become jaded,

00:42:36.279 --> 00:42:37.746
to treat the extraordinary

00:42:37.781 --> 00:42:40.113
like just another day
at the office.

00:42:40.150 --> 00:42:42.914
But sometimes...

00:42:42.953 --> 00:42:46.980
there are experiences
which transcend all that.

00:42:47.024 --> 00:42:48.924
You've just had one, Mr. Kim,

00:42:48.959 --> 00:42:53.225
and I want you to live
with it for a little while.

00:42:53.263 --> 00:42:55.231
Write about it
if you feel like it.

00:42:55.265 --> 00:42:57.324
Paint...

00:42:57.367 --> 00:42:59.562
express yourself
in some fashion.

00:42:59.603 --> 00:43:02.572
The Bridge will still be there
in two days.

00:43:02.606 --> 00:43:05.541
Thank you, Captain.

00:43:05.575 --> 00:43:10.945
I have been a little preoccupied
with the experience.

00:43:11.048 --> 00:43:12.879
I mean, all those people think

00:43:12.916 --> 00:43:15.384
that they know
what happens after death.

00:43:15.419 --> 00:43:16.784
They look forward to it.

00:43:16.820 --> 00:43:18.788
They're prepared for it.

00:43:18.822 --> 00:43:22.781
But the truth is,
none of it's real.

00:43:22.826 --> 00:43:25.386
They don't have an afterlife.

00:43:25.429 --> 00:43:28.398
They just decay
inside those asteroids.

00:43:28.432 --> 00:43:31.333
I wouldn't be so sure of that
if I were you.

00:43:31.368 --> 00:43:34.166
That neural energy
their bodies release...

00:43:34.204 --> 00:43:35.637
it becomes part

00:43:35.672 --> 00:43:39.540
of the ambient electromagnetic
field surrounding the planet.

00:43:39.576 --> 00:43:41.601
Our readings also indicate

00:43:41.645 --> 00:43:43.977
the energy is unusually dynamic.

00:43:44.081 --> 00:43:46.379
There's a great deal
of variation

00:43:46.416 --> 00:43:49.249
in pattern complexity,
quantum density...

00:43:49.286 --> 00:43:53.552
Are you saying you think
they do have an afterlife?

00:43:53.590 --> 00:43:56.559
That the energy field
is where they exist

00:43:56.593 --> 00:43:58.891
at a higher level
of consciousness,

00:43:58.929 --> 00:44:00.590
just like they believe?

00:44:02.599 --> 00:44:05.067
I'm not certain.

00:44:05.102 --> 00:44:08.071
But I am certain about this:

00:44:08.105 --> 00:44:12.064
What we don't know about death

00:44:12.109 --> 00:44:16.341
is far, far greater
than what we do know.

00:44:18.048 --> 00:44:20.949
See you in two days, Ensign.

00:44:21.051 --> 00:44:23.212
Thank you, Captain.
